The playbook with the one-line proofs:

```css
/* OVERFLOW — find the culprit visually */
* { outline: 1px solid rgba(255, 0, 0, 0.35); }  /* border would shift layout */
/* then fix by cause: */
.page   { width: 100%; }            /* NOT 100vw — vw includes the scrollbar */
.grid-item { min-width: 0; }       /* flex/grid children refuse to shrink
                                        below min-content without this */
.long-word { overflow-wrap: anywhere; }  /* unbreakable strings */
.hero   { width: min(1100px, 100% - 2rem); }  /* responsive + bounded */

/* STACKING — the parent is the problem, not the child */
.modal-host { position: relative; z-index: 40; }  /* raise the CONTEXT */
/* z-index works ONLY on: position != static, flex items, grid items */
/* NEW CONTEXTS: position+z-index, transform, filter, opacity < 1,
   will-change, isolation: isolate, contain: paint */

/* STICKY — the three requirements */
.sticky-header {
  position: sticky;
  top: 0;                         /* 1. an offset — required */
}
/* 2. the PARENT must be taller than the sticky (room to stick within)
   3. no overflow: hidden/auto ancestor between it and the scrollport
      — a mid-ancestor with overflow becomes the scroll container it
        sticks against (usually the surprise) */

/* MARGIN COLLAPSE — siblings' vertical margins merge */
.a { margin-bottom: 24px; }  .b { margin-top: 16px; }  /* gap: 24px not 40 */
/* fixes: flex/grid parent (never collapses), padding/border on the
   parent, or the modern: gap on flex/grid, margin never collapses there */
```

The method (same as any debugging): reproduce at the exact width/zoom, outline ALL boxes to see the truth, then walk the CAUSE checklist — the four families cover the vast majority of layout bug reports. The payoff of knowing the stacking-context list cold: 'modal behind header' takes 30 seconds instead of an afternoon of z-index escalation — you look at the ancestor chain for the context creators and fix the ONE parent that matters.
